  "related_identifiers": null,
  "description_H9_excerpts": [
    "<p class=\"code-line\"><strong>(11,5), 37,628.</strong>&nbsp;A partial fold of H(9), built on the construction and duality data of R. Rajiv. A closed split set, 29 copies of H(3) and 122 pencil vertices give a graph on 37,622 vertices. Six further vertices are added, each joined to vertices with a free degree slot (50 new edges). No vertex or edge of the 37,622-vertex graph is removed.</p>",
    "<p class=\"code-line\"><strong>(12,5), 42,342.</strong>&nbsp;A partial fold of H(9), built on the construction and duality data of R. Rajiv: a closed split set, copies of H(3) and pencil vertices. A further 165 vertices are added, each joined to at most 12 vertices with a free degree slot, so that the balls of radius 4 around their neighbours cover the graph.</p>",
    "<p class=\"code-line\"><strong>(13,5), 51,417.</strong>&nbsp;A partial fold of H(9) on R. Rajiv's (13,5) split set. The pencil vertices carry extra anchors, and twin vertices fill the free slots that remain.</p>"
  ],
